PART 3.  THE ARBITER: exact W against both candidate first-order slopes
================================================================================================
  dW/dtheta at theta->0 must equal (1/2) Tr(M_11 Y). The competing
  pure-branch endpoints are (theta/2) Delta_H * spread(Y)  [paper]
  and (theta/4) Delta_H * spread(Y)  [referee].

  case                             exact dW/dth   (1/2)Tr(M11 Y)   paper end  referee end
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  n=1  H=Z  Y=X  tau=0.7            -0.49272486      -0.49272486    1.000000     0.500000
  n=2  H=ZZ+X1  Y=X1+X2              0.15928383       0.15928383    2.644095     1.322048
  n=3  H=Heis chain  Y=sum X        -0.00000000      -0.00000000    4.580931     2.290465

  The first two columns agreeing confirms the chain identity -> M_11 -> W.
  The endpoint columns are the MAXIMUM |dW/dtheta| over the isospectral
  orbit of Y, so the true slope must not exceed the correct one, and the
  incorrect one will be exceeded by orbit-optimal configurations.
